cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PartnerQC, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PartnerQC: glucose as a built-in partner for patient-based quality control of HbA1c"
abstract: >-
  PartnerQC checks every glycated haemoglobin (HbA1c) result against the glucose
  measured in the same sample. HbA1c and glucose quantiles follow a power law with a
  stable exponent across populations, so the partner spread
  ln(HbA1c) - beta * ln(glucose) removes much of the between-patient variation and an
  exponentially weighted moving average of it detects HbA1c analyser bias between
  internal quality control runs. The software provides an offline web app, a Python
  package and command-line tool, and an HTTP service for laboratory information
  system integration.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
keywords:
  - glycated haemoglobin
  - HbA1c
  - glucose
  - patient-based real-time quality control
  - PBRTQC
  - internal quality control
  - laboratory quality management
